{"title":"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 12","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Problem\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Problem</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Solutions\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solutions</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Solution_1\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 1</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Solution_2\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 2</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Solution_3(elimination)\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 3(elimination)</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Solution_4\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Solution 4</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-8\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>Suppose that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the product of three consecutive integers and that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />. Which of the following is not necessarily a divisor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" />?\n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/5/8/1/581f86f7c5d8ba57ce9b07f201e6efc2afd18602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ 6 \\qquad \\textbf{(B)}\\ 14 \\qquad \\textbf{(C)}\\ 21 \\qquad \\textbf{(D)}\\ 28 \\qquad \\textbf{(E)}\\ 42$\" style=\"vertical-align: -4px\" width=\"385\" height=\"17\" />\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solutions\">Solutions</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solutions\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_1\">Solution 1</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 1\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Whenever <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is the product of three consecutive integers, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/8/5/6859713adc973d3fbe97fafef9ce829757e54b12.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$3!$\" width=\"12\" height=\"13\" />, meaning it is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/0/1/601a7806cbfad68196c43a4665871f8c3186802e.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />.\n</p><p>It also mentions that it is divisible by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/0/a/e0a0db32027a732ac57d37ef2ae9bb150f65b108.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"14\" />, so the number is definitely divisible by all the factors of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" />.\n</p><p>In our answer choices, the one that is not a factor of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/d/0/ed0d6c36fdad9c2874053be46c7e4120f2edcf47.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"17\" height=\"12\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72f47668e3864cedcd7c57b2a6de70a3e9c1477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_2\">Solution 2</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 2\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>We can look for counterexamples. For example, letting <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/1/9/4196fb83c13b406206acd2b326385ab5fd099d38.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 13 \\cdot 14 \\cdot 15$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"115\" height=\"13\" />, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/7/4/174fadd07fd54c9afe288e96558c92e0c1da733a.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"13\" height=\"10\" /> is not divisible by 28, so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/d/e/3deff89e67ca3b645654e0c553e3563ae33df908.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D) }28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"67\" height=\"30\" /> is our answer.\n</p>\n<h3><span id=\"Solution_3.28elimination.29\"></span><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_3(elimination)\">Solution 3(elimination)</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 3(elimination)\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>No matter what 3 integers you choose, one of them has to be even, so since <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/6/5/66556d6b32c530806d96c5a650c399c32636eb15.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$14 = 7 \\cdot 2$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />, and it has 7 and 2 as a divisor, answer B is out. Now, if it wasn't divisible by 3, it could be A or C(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/b/f/dbff1a0f9e72e610eecd4043bb943ac9b5f3d510.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$21 = 7 \\cdot 3$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />,and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/b/1/4b14f6e455da1b3cc8dbdb14653345f8de0c37db.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$6 = 2 \\cdot 3$\" width=\"64\" height=\"12\" />)m so it must be divisible by 3. Therefore, it is either D or E. Since we eliminated 6, if it was E, it would be not divisible by 6(<img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/8/358ecbad601252f439d7b84e88e5bd46c4eb9ab0.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$42 = 7 \\cdot 6$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"76\" height=\"14\" />), but it is not, so the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72f47668e3864cedcd7c57b2a6de70a3e9c1477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~idk12345678\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution_4\">Solution 4</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Solution 4\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Let <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/6/1/d61ddf2d83f476b8cdda9f0c3659916edbc2069b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = a \\cdot (a + 1) \\cdot (a + 2)$\" style=\"vertical-align: -5px\" width=\"183\" height=\"20\" />. Minimizing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/7/d/c7d457e388298246adb06c587bccd419ea67f7e8.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"11\" height=\"10\" /> so that 7 is a factor, we see that when <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72e2e58a2ef8bb4eedd627c212f63bb8f507301.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$a = 5$\" width=\"42\" height=\"12\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/a/d/0/ad01e28656f469958ab41289361a6fa23c0802d7.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$n = 5 \\cdot 6 \\cdot 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"91\" height=\"14\" />. Taking the prime factorization of this, we see that you cannot make 28 from <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/1/e/d1e002fe44ca478d18bcf056ab49ac0f7856f602.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$2 \\cdot 3 \\cdot 5 \\cdot 7$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"78\" height=\"14\" />. Therefore, the answer is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/7/2/e72f47668e3864cedcd7c57b2a6de70a3e9c1477.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(D)}\\ 28}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -10px\" width=\"65\" height=\"28\" />.\n</p><p>~ mohizoid\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Video_Solution_by_Daily_Dose_of_Math\">Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: Video Solution by Daily Dose of Math\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external free\" href=\"https://youtu.be/Ce2zWT2A0sU?si=FxjhpB2Tq0vHcl9B\">https://youtu.be/Ce2zWT2A0sU?si=FxjhpB2Tq0vHcl9B</a>\n</p><p>~Thesmartgreekmathdude\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_12&amp;action=edit&amp;section=8\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 10\">2001 AMC 10</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Answer_Key\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/community/c13\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 11\">Problem 11</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 13\">Problem 13</a></b>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_1\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 1\">1</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_2\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 2\">2</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_3\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 3\">3</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_4\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 4\">4</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_5\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 5\">5</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_6\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 6\">6</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_7\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 7\">7</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_8\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 8\">8</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_9\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 9\">9</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_10\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 10\">10</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_11\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 11\">11</a> <b>•</b> <a class=\"mw-selflink selflink\">12</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_13\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 13\">13</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_14\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 14\">14</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_15\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 15\">15</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_16\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 16\">16</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_17\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 17\">17</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_18\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 18\">18</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_19\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 19\">19</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_20\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 20\">20</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_21\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 21\">21</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_22\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 22\">22</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_23\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 23\">23</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_24\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 24\">24</a> <b>•</b> <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=2001_AMC_10_Problems/Problem_25\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"2001 AMC 10 Problems/Problem 25\">25</a>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td colspan=\"3\" style=\"text-align:center;\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=AMC_10_Problems_and_Solutions\" title=\"AMC 10 Problems and Solutions\"> All AMC 10 Problems and Solutions</a></b>\n</td></tr></tbody></table>\n<div class=\"print\">\n<div style=\"display:flex;width:100%;justify-content:space-between;align-items:center\">\n<div>\n<p><span class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File\"><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=File:AMC_Logo.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\"><img src=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/images/d/d1/AMC_Logo.png\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"97\" height=\"84\" class=\"mw-file-element\" /></a></span>\n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"flex-grow:1;text-align:right\">\n<p>These problems are copyrighted &#169; by the <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://www.maa.org\">Mathematical Association of America</a>. \n</p>\n</div>\n<div style=\"clear:both;\"></div>\n</div></div>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017193631\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.037 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.060 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 243/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 2294/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 128/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 3/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 4895/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%   13.673      1 -total\n 62.43%    8.536      1 Template:AMC10_box\n 36.55%    4.997      1 Template:MAA_Notice\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:9149:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017193631 and revision id 263428. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}